 1. Time.utc(2024, 2, 29, 12); class; utc?; zone               2024-02-29 12:00:00 UTC; Time; true; UTC
 2. + 86400 adds seconds; later - t is a Float of seconds      2024-03-01 12:00:00 UTC; 86400.0 (Float)
 3. + 0.5 keeps subseconds (inspect shows them); usec          2024-02-29 12:00:00.5 UTC; 500000
 4. strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %z"); ("%A %d %B %Y")          2024-02-29 12:00:00 +0000; Thursday 29 February 2024
 5. strftime("%j %U %u %I %p %-d %e|")  (%-d and %e are Ruby's own) 060 08 4 12 PM 29 29|
 6. iso8601 and xmlschema are core methods in 4.0 (no require) 2024-02-29T12:00:00Z; 2024-02-29T12:00:00Z; 2024-02-29T12:00:00.000Z
 7. to_i, to_f, to_r are seconds since the epoch               1709208000; 1709208000.0; 1709208000/1
 8. Time.at(0) is local time (TZ=UTC here): utc? is false; .utc 1970-01-01 00:00:00 +0000; false; 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC
 9. Time.new(2024, 2, 29, 12) is local: utc?; zone; == t       2024-02-29 12:00:00 +0000; false; UTC; true
10. Time.new(..., in: "+02:00"); getutc; utc_offset; == t      2024-02-29 12:00:00 +0200; 2024-02-29 10:00:00 UTC; 7200; false
11. t.getlocal("+02:00") is the same instant shown elsewhere   2024-02-29 14:00:00 +0200; hour=14; == t: true
12. t <=> t + 1; == and eql? with an equal Time; equal?        -1; true; true; false
13. Time.utc(2024, 2, 30) rolls over; hour 25 does not         2024-03-01 00:00:00 UTC; ArgumentError: hour out of range
14. (t + 0.5).round; t.to_a                                    2024-02-29 12:00:01 UTC; [0, 0, 12, 29, 2, 2024, 4, 60, false, "UTC"]
15. Time.parse/iso8601/strptime need require "time": before, after false, true
16. Time.iso8601("2024-02-29T12:00:00+02:00").utc; Time.strptime 2024-02-29 10:00:00 UTC; 2024-02-29 00:00:00 +0000
17. Time.new also parses a String (3.2+)                       2024-02-29 12:00:00 UTC
18. Date.new(2024, 1, 31); + 1 is a day; >> 1 is a month (clamped) 2024-01-31; 2024-02-01; 2024-02-29; 2025-02-28; 2023-12-31
19. Date - Date is a Rational number of days                   (30/1) (Rational); to_i=30
20. Date.parse, Date.iso8601, Date.strptime                    2024-03-01; 2024-03-01; 2024-03-01
21. Date.leap?(2024, 2100, 2000); valid_date?(2024, 2, 30); Date.new [true, false, true]; false; Date::Error: invalid date
22. wday (Sunday=0), cwday (Monday=1), yday, cweek; DAYNAMES[wday] 3; 3; 31; 5; Wednesday
23. a negative day counts from the end: Date.new(2024, 2, -1)  2024-02-29; 2023-02-28
24. a Range of Dates; step                                     ["2024-01-01", "2024-01-02", "2024-01-03"]; ["2024-01-01", "2024-01-04", "2024-01-07", "2024-01-10"]
25. Date#to_time is local midnight; Time#to_date               2024-01-31 00:00:00 +0000; 2024-02-29 (Date)
26. DateTime exists (DateTime < Date) but Time is the one to use 2024-02-29T12:00:00+00:00; superclass=Date
27. Time and Date deconstruct_keys for pattern matching (3.2+) {year: 2024, month: 2}; matched, hour=12
